# Example environment file for the dashboard's Vite build (see
# src/services/forgedbApi.ts). Copy this to a local, untracked `.env`
# only if you want to point a local production-mode build (`npm run
# build && npm run preview`) at a real deployed ForgeDB endpoint
# instead of Vite's dev-only proxy.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# On Vercel, set this as a Project Settings -> Environment Variable
# instead of committing a file -- Vite inlines VITE_-prefixed variables
# into the built JS at build time, so this is never read at runtime and
# never belongs in a tracked file once it holds a real deployment's
# hostname.
#
# Leave unset for local `npm run dev`: forgedbApi.ts falls back to the
# relative '/api' path, which vite.config.ts's dev-only proxy forwards
# to a local ForgeDB node.
#
# VITE_FORGEDB_API_BASE_URL=https://your-stable-hostname.example.com

# Optional, local `npm run dev` only -- NOT a VITE_-prefixed variable, so
# Vite never inlines it into the built JS bundle (see vite.config.ts's
# proxy `configure` comment). A ForgeDB node run locally or via
# docker-compose.yml requires every protected endpoint to carry
# `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (/health and /ready are the only
# exceptions -- see internal/api/auth.go); without this set, the
# dashboard's "live" Cluster/KV/Observability views can reach /health but
# get 401 from /cluster, /kv/*, and /metrics. Set this to the same value
# as this repo's root .env's FORGEDB_API_TOKEN so the dev proxy can attach
# it server-side. Never set a real production token here if this file is
# ever copied into a build pipeline that inlines non-prefixed vars --
# this mechanism is for the local dev proxy only, never for a deployed
# build (e.g. Vercel), which has no server-side proxy to attach it.
#
# FORGEDB_API_TOKEN=replace-with-the-same-value-as-the-root-.env
